.TH READLINK 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
readlink \- print the target of a symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readlink
.I path
.RI [ path ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readlink
prints the raw target text stored in each symbolic link named by a
.I path
operand, one per line, exactly as stored \(em it is not canonicalized,
resolved relative to any directory, or checked for existence. Multiple
operands are processed in turn; a failure on one operand does not stop
the rest from being attempted.
.PP
No options are recognized; every command-line argument, including one
that begins with
.BR \- ,
is treated as a
.I path
operand.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I path
A pathname of a symbolic link.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The target of every
.I path
operand was printed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A
.I path
operand did not exist, was not a symbolic link, or its target could
not otherwise be read; the rest of the operands were still attempted.
Also used if writing a result to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
No
.I path
operand was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR realpath (1),
.BR ln (1)
